By the way:

When you find a gray stone that isn't a loadstone, you can find out if
it is a luckstone immediately by trying to #name it "The Heart of
Ahriman"

If your hand slips, it is a luckstone, if it doesn't you can try
rubbing it on an iron weapon or armor, and if it makes a "scritch,
scritch" sound then it is a touchstone, otherwise it is a flint stone.

You don't need to cast identify on it.


